          "comments": "Synthetic all-passing fixture for hdf-libs regression test - pins safe behavior to prevent empty-requirements regression.",
          "finding_details": "",
          "srg_id": "SRG-APP-000456"
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-251546",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-251546",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000560",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-251546",
          "severity": "high",
          "group_title": "Firefox must be configured to allow only TLS 1.2 or above.",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-251546r961869_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-251546r961869",
          "rule_version": "FFOX-00-000002",
          "rule_title": "Firefox must be configured to allow only TLS 1.2 or above.",
          "fix_text": "Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Minimum SSL version enabled\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value: TLS 1.2   (or TLS 1.3)\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n<key>SSLVersionMin</key>\n<string>tls1.2</string>   (or <string>tls1.3</string>)\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"SSLVersionMin\": \"tls1.2\"   or (\"SSLVersionMin\": \"tls1.3\")",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window. \n\nIf \"SSLVersionMin\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"tls1.2\" or \"tls1.3\", this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Mozilla_Firefox_2021_VERSION_STIG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Use of versions prior to TLS 1.2 are not permitted. SSL 2.0 and SSL 3.0 contain a number of security flaws. These versions must be disabled in compliance with the Network Infrastructure and Secure Remote Computing STIGs.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-001453"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5446",
          "uuid": "36db5946-11ce-4072-baf0-6f8798ca925d",
          "stig_uuid": "add7e8af-33db-420d-aeb6-923f648b0698",
          "status": "not_a_finding",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Synthetic all-passing fixture for hdf-libs regression test - pins safe behavior to prevent empty-requirements regression.",
          "finding_details": "",
          "srg_id": "SRG-APP-000560"
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-251547",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-251547",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000177",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-251547",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "Firefox must be configured to ask which certificate to present to a website when a certificate is required.",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-251547r1067550_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-251547r1067550",
          "rule_version": "FFOX-00-000003",
          "rule_title": "Firefox must be configured to ask which certificate to present to a website when a certificate is required.",
          "fix_text": "Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Preferences\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value:\n{\n  \"security.default_personal_cert\": {\n    \"Value\": \"Ask Every Time\",\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n<key>Preferences</key>\n<dict>\n  <key>security.default_personal_cert</key>\n  <dict>\n    <key>Value</key>\n    <string>Ask Every Time</string>\n    <key>Status</key>\n    <string>locked</string>\n  </dict>\n</dict>\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"Preferences\": {\n  \"security.default_personal_cert\": {\n    \"Value\": \"Ask Every Time\",\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"Preferences\" is not displayed under Policy Name and the Policy Value does not include \"security.default_personal_cert\" with a value of \"Ask Every Time\" and status of \"locked\", this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Mozilla_Firefox_2021_VERSION_STIG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "When a website asks for a certificate for user authentication, Firefox must be configured to have the user choose which certificate to present. Websites within DOD require user authentication for access, which increases security for DOD information. Access will be denied to the user if certificate management is not configured.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000187"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5446",
